he modern city-state.\"\n\nSo the documents do mention Vatican City (Paragraph 18 and 19), and Paragraph 4 mentions that Pope John XXIII was sovereign of Vatican City.\n\nThe specific answer from the documents would be:\n- Pope John XXIII died on 3 June 1963\n- He was sovereign of Vatican City during his reign (1958-1963)\n- The location \"Vatican City\" is mentioned in the documents (Paragraph 18)\n\nHowever, the documents don't explicitly state WHERE he died - only that he was sovereign of Vatican City.\n</think>\n\nBased on the documents provided:\n\n**Where Pope John XXIII died:**\nAccording to the documents, Pope John XXIII died on **3 June 1963** (Paragraph 4). He reigned from **1958 to 1963** as sovereign of **Vatican City**.\n\n**Is the location mentioned in the documents?**\nYes, **Vatican City** is mentioned in the documents:\n- In Paragraph 4, it states Pope John XXIII was \"sovereign of Vatican City\" from 1958 to 1963\n- In Paragraph 18, there's a detailed paragraph about Vatican City, explaining its origin from the Lateran Treaty signed on 11 February 1929\n\n**Answer Summary:**\n1. Pope John XXIII died on 3 June 1963 in **Vatican City** (inferred from his status as sovereign of Vatican City during his reign 1958-1963)\n2. Yes, Vatican City is explicitly mentioned in the documents\n\nNote: While the documents establish Vatican City as the location associated with Pope John XXIII's papacy and sovereignty, they don't contain an explicit statement like \"Pope John XXIII died in Vatican City.\" The city itself is referenced in multiple paragraphs.\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_21bf15bb3ffebtFkfVfCf4QWV7","model":{"modelID":"qwen35-9b","providerID":"local"},"truncated":false},"title":"Find Pope John XXIII death location","time":{"start":1777647658057,"end":1777647688071}}}}
